---
/*
  Home. Structure and copy: 04-konzept.md section 4.3, page "/".
  Six sections, one message above the fold, no number tiles, no badges.

  DECIDED (Manuel, 07.09.2026, abends): the revenue split is NOT stated on the
  public site. It is covered in the closing call. This replaces the earlier
  decision from midday. Do not put a split figure back on any page.
  DECIDED (Manuel, 07.09.2026): no contract term, notice period or renewal
  language on the site. Early exit if it stops working stays, without a
  concrete deadline.
  DECIDED (Manuel, 07.09.2026, abends): most creators are not native English
  speakers. Every sentence on this page is short and plain on purpose. The
  build measures it, see scripts/check-copy.mjs, rule 5.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../components/CtaBlock.astro';
import RecordCard from '../components/RecordCard.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { legal } from '../site';

const records = (await getCollection('records'))
  .filter((entry) => !entry.data.draft)
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
const firstRecord = records[0];
---

<Base
  title="Wunder | Managed against your own numbers"
  description="Wunder is a creator management company in Riga. We write down what your account did in the last thirty days. After that, you measure us against that number."
>
  <section class="section hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div>
          <h1>Managed against your own numbers.</h1>
          <p class="lead">
            Wunder is a creator management company. We are based in Riga. Before we start, we look
            at your last thirty days. We write that number down. Then you measure us against it.
            You see the same portal we do.
          </p>
          <CtaBlock secondary />
        </div>
        <Photo
          file="lauris-kalnins.webp"
          alt="Lauris Kalnins sits at a desk with a laptop and an open notebook."
          width={900}
          height={1349}
          sizes="(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 420px"
          ratio="portrait"
          eager
          caption="Lauris Kalnins, COO. He runs the day to day work with our creators."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>You know what your account did at its best.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        We write that number down before we start. Then you can hold us to it.
      </p>
      {
        firstRecord ? (
          <div class="record-slot">
            <RecordCard {...firstRecord.data} />
          </div>
        ) : (
          <div class="record-slot panel">
            <p>
              Six creators tell you on video what changed for them. Watch them on the
              <a href="/results">results page</a>.
            </p>
            <p class="caption">
              Our own case cards are not ready yet. We check each one against the portal first.
            </p>
          </div>
        )
      }
      <p class="caption">
        Every result here is one case. Each one has a date. Each one says what did not work.
        <a href="/proof">See how we report numbers</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Why you are on this page.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Most people come to us for one of four things. Growth that has stopped. Help with the work
        that is not the content. Marketing skills they never had time to learn. Or free time. We
        will not guess which one is yours. Tell us on the call.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Three things we can show you, not just tell you.</h2>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="panel">
          <h3>You see the same screen we do</h3>
          <p>
            Every post goes through our own system. We read each number at the source. We do not
            guess it. You log into your own portal. There you see views, reach and followers. You
            can look at seven, thirty and ninety days.
          </p>
          <p><a href="/how-it-works#portal">See how it works</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3>You never hand us a password</h3>
          <p>
            We post to Instagram through Zernio. We run the OnlyFans chat and vault through
            Infloww. Both are official tools. You give them access, and you can take it back. A
            password you hand over is gone.
          </p>
          <p><a href="/how-it-works#access">See how it works</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3>We check the people who write in your name</h3>
          <p>
            Twice a week our system reads the last finished shift. It scores the chat against a
            written rule set. The check runs to a fixed plan. Nobody on the chat team can turn it
            off.
          </p>
          <p>
            We write down who writes to your fans. You may say that in your own bio. We will not
            ask you to take it down.
          </p>
          <p><a href="/how-it-works#chatting">See how it works</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>How you get paid.</h2>
      <p>
        There is no setup fee. There is no minimum you have to earn. OnlyFans pays your own bank
        first. We send our bill after that, once a week. We go through the numbers on the call.
        You sign nothing before that.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can leave early if this stops working for you. We show you how on the call.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your content stays yours. We never held your passwords. So there is nothing to hand back.
        We switch your portal access off the same day.
      </p>
      <CtaBlock />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>A real company, with two people who sign for it.</h2>
      <p>
        Wunder is a brand by {legal.company}. The number in the register is {legal.regNumber}. The
        company started in Riga on {legal.registered}. Two directors run it, and each one may sign
        alone. Manuel Gonzalez is CEO and co owner. Lauris Kalnins is COO and co owner.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can look all of that up first. <a href="/company">The company page has the rest</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Apply, and we tell you either way.</h2>
      <p>
        You send eight short answers. A person reads them. Then you hear if it is a fit. If it is
        not, you get one line. You do not get silence.
      </p>
      <p>We answer within one working day.</p>
      <CtaBlock secondary />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-top: 88px;
  }

  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.3fr 1fr;
    gap: 56px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .record-slot {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 32px 0 24px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero {
      padding-top: 48px;
    }
    .hero-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 32px;
    }
  }
</style>
